**How to implement.** AT-2's data are the harness's noisy observations, written as kit data files through the observation profile and read back through it (001 §Q AT-2 'Data: for each of the five seeds, the observations come from the EXISTING `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith forward absorbing NoiseParam.decentLab seed fullConfigurations`; they are written as kit data files under `data/absorbing-biaxial-noisy/data/` through the Mueller-matrix import profile, committed with the kit, and read back through the same profile; the test regenerates them from the seeds and requires the committed files byte-identical'; steps 301, 317-320, 340). The observation file is what the bench's instrument writes, so the build writes it into the kit's `data/`, as AT-1's lab files lie there, and the app attaches it in place (step 134). Each private function is documented in one line citing spec 0050 S12.2. (1) `noisyObservationsOf (seed : NoiseSeed) : MuellerObservation list`: `noisyObserveAbsoluteWith (MuellerInverse.createBerremanForward (fun (p : AbsorbingTriclinicParameters) -> p.opticalProperties) BiaxialSample.solverParameters) AbsorbingBiaxialSample.absorbing NoiseParam.decentLab seed AbsorbingBiaxialSample.fullConfigurations` (step 340; the forward `AbsorbingBiaxialNoisyTests` draws with, step 334), an `Error` failing the fact naming the seed and the error. `plateLabelOf (cut : SampleCut) : ItemLabel` is step 433's table read the other way. `observationFileOf (seed : NoiseSeed) : KitFileText` is `KeyedObservation.observationFileText` (step 301) of `noisyObservationsOf seed` in the harness's order, each keyed `DataRowKey` of its plate's label, an `Error` failing the fact. (2) `buildAbsorbingKit` continues: for each seed of `AbsorbingBiaxialSample.noisySeeds` (step 431) in order, the built folder's `data/noisy-observations-seed-<n>.csv`, `n` the seed's value, is written with the text of `observationFileOf seed` exactly (LF, no byte-order mark: the text's own); then, through the window's messages, `SplitByColumn (FileName <seed 1's file, absolute>, ImportProfileName.muellerObservations)` (step 319; the profile splits by `sample`, step 317), whose five groups are each `ExperimentForGroup` of the experiment its key names (step 318 (b)), and `MatchByTemplate` (step 320), which records the file in place and gives each experiment `KeyedDataRows` of its key. The other four files stay in `data/` unattached: the ensemble attaches them in turn (step 437), and the equality of step 438 compares them. (3) The fact `AT-2 writes each seed's noisy observations through the Mueller-matrix observation profile and attaches seed 1's to its plates`: after the build, the built folder's `data/` holds exactly the five files, each byte-identical to `observationFileOf` of its seed regenerated in the fact, and each read back by `parseMuellerObservations` (step 301) to its seed's observations keyed by plate: every configuration equal and every `measured.element i j` equal exactly to `noisyObservationsOf`'s; a second `KitProxy.create` reads each experiment with `dataOpt` the attachment `data/noisy-observations-seed-1.csv` at that file's SHA-256, profile `Mueller-matrix observations`, `KeyedDataRows (DataRowKey <the experiment's name>)` and no exclusion; and the window's `experimentData.readMapped` (step 305) reads each to `ObservationPoints` of its plate's seed-1 observations in file order. The step-432 and step-433 facts keep their assertions.

**Acceptance.** After AT-2's third part lands, the build MUST write the five seeds' observation files into the kit's `data/` through `KeyedObservation.observationFileText`, each reading back through the profile to its seed's observations exactly, and attach seed 1's file in place to the five experiments by its `sample` key; kit-acceptance MUST pass over `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.KitAcceptanceTests`, including `AT-2 writes each seed's noisy observations through the Mueller-matrix observation profile and attaches seed 1's to its plates`, the count rising by 1; and build, elevation and the twenty-one s42 invariants MUST pass.
